---
import { RpnLab } from "../../components/RpnLab.tsx";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteNav from "../../components/SiteNav.astro";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { url } from "../../lib/urls";
import "../../styles/docs.css";
import "../../components/RpnLab.css";
import "@ovh/depth-ui/src/stage.css";
import "../../components/Explorer.css";
---

<Base
  domain="algorithms"
  title="A stack machine, running — OpenLabs"
  description="A reverse Polish calculator modelled as parts: a tape, a belt, a dispatcher, a stack and an operator. Type an expression and watch the items move."
>
  <SiteNav current="labs" />

  <main id="content">
    <section class="lab-head editorial">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lab-head__eyebrow mono">
          <a href={url("handbooks/algorithms")}>Algorithms Visual Handbook</a> ·
          lab
        </p>
        <h1>A stack machine, running</h1>
        <p>
          Postfix notation puts the operator after its two values:
          <span class="mono">3 4 +</span> is seven. There are no parentheses,
          because the order already is the grouping. That is the whole trick,
          and it is why a machine can evaluate it with one stack and no
          lookahead.
        </p>
        <p>
          The stack here is not a variable hidden in some code. It is a box on
          the screen with its contents visible and its top marked, and the
          number that lands in it got there by travelling: out of the tape,
          along the belt, through the dispatcher that asks "value or operator?"
          — and back down from the operator over the clock edge.
        </p>
        <p>
          The pacing is the part worth watching. Nothing schedules the tape: the
          stack asks for the next symbol only once it has applied the last one.
          Two operators in a row therefore cannot run into each other, and a
          longer expression costs more ticks because there is more work, not
          because a timer was turned down.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="lab-head__note mono">
        <p>One stack. No parentheses.</p>
        <p>The belt costs a tick, like a belt does.</p>
        <p>Divide by zero and it says so.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-stage">
      <RpnLab client:only="react" />
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .lab-head {
    padding-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-2);
  }

  .lab-head__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-1);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: var(--size-step--1);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--size-step-3);
    max-width: 16ch;
  }

  .lab-head__note {
    align-self: end;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--size-step--1);
  }

  .lab-head__note p {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
  }

  .lab-stage {
    max-width: 96rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-3) var(--space-5);
  }
</style>
